    <h1> simple omelette recipe </h1>
    <aside>
        <p> An easy and quick dish,perfecrt for any meal. This classic omelette combiness beaten eggs cooked to perfect, optionally filled with your choise of cheese, vegetables, or meats </p>
    </aside>
    <h2>prepration time </h2> 
    <nav>
        <ul>
            <li><span class="title">Total:</span>
                Approximately 10 minutes
            </li>
            <li> <span class="title"> prepration:</span>
                5 minutes
            </li>
            <li><span class="title"> Cooking</span> 
                 5 minutes
            </li>
        </ul>
    </nav>
    <h3> Ingredients </h3>
    <nav>
        <ul>
            <li>2-3large eggs</li>
            <li> salt,to taste</li>
            <li>pepper,to taste</li>
            <li> 1 tablespon of butter or oil</li>
            <li> optional filling: cheese, diced vegetables, cooked meats, herbs</li>
    </nav>
    <h4> Instructions </h4>
    <nav>
        <ol>
            <li> <span class="title">Beat the eggss:</span> 
                 in a bowl,beat the eggs with a pinch of salt and pepper until they are well mixed. You can add a tablespoon of water or milk for a fluffier texture
                </li>
            <li> <span class="title">Heat the pan;</span>
                 Place a non-stick frying pan over medium heat and add butter or oil
                 </li>
            <li> <span class="title">Cook the omelette:</span>
                 Once the butter is melted and bubbling,pour in the eggs. Tilt the pan to ensure the eggs evenly coat the surface
                </li>
            <li><span class="title">  Add fillings(optional):</span>
                When the eggs begin to set at the endges but are still slightly runny in the midle , sprinkle your chosen fillings over one hakf of the omelette
            </li>
            <li> <span class="title"> Fold and serve:</span>
                 As thew omelette continues to cook , carfully lift ona edge and fold it over the fillings. Let it cook for another minute , then slide it onto a plate
                </li>
            <li> <span class="title">Enjoy:</span>
                 Serve hot, with additional salt and pepper if needed
                </li>
        </ol>
    </nav>
